<div class="section-component parbase aem-GridColumn aem-GridColumn--default--12">
    <div class=" veeam-component__component-spacing-below--sm">
        <div class="section    " style="background-image: linear-gradient(180deg, transparent 0.0%, transparent 100.0%); border-color: #b0b0b0;">
            <div class="bg-image-size-contain bg-image-position-left      ">
                <div class="  " style="max-width: 100%;">
<div class="aem-Grid aem-Grid--12 aem-Grid--default--12 ">
    <div class="section-title-component aem-GridColumn aem-GridColumn--default--12">
<div class="section-title left 
            section-title--only-title  ">
    <div class="section-title__title-block">
        <h2 class="section-title__title">
            Issue Details
        </h2>
    </div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="veeam-text text aem-GridColumn aem-GridColumn--default--12">
    <div class=" veeam-component__component-spacing-below--lg">
    <div class="veeam-text  veeam-text--adaptive-mode" data-component="VeeamTextComponent">
        <h4><b>CVE-2026-107239</b></h4>
<p>A vulnerability allowing a member of the Veeam Virtualization Extensions Users group to perform remote code execution (RCE) on servers running the Veeam Management Pack <i>for Microsoft System Center</i> Collector service.</p>
<p><b>Severity:</b> High<br><b>CVSS v4.0 Score:</b> <span class="veeam-tooltip">8.8<span class="veeam-tooltip-text">CVSS: AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:L/UI:P/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:H/SI:L/SA:L</span></span><br><b>Source:</b> Discovered during internal testing.</p>
<h5><b>Affected Product</b></h5>
<ul>
 <li>Veeam Management Pack <i>for Microsoft System Center</i> 9.1 and all earlier version 9 builds, including the <a href="https://www.veeam.com/kb4876" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Veeam Backup & Replication 13 compatibility patch</a>.<br><sub><b>Note:</b> A fix will not be provided for version 9.x. Customers running version 9.x should upgrade to 13.1.0.334.</sub><br><sub><b>Note:</b> <a href="https://www.veeam.com/product-lifecycle.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Unsupported product versions</a> were not tested, but are likely affected and should be considered vulnerable.</sub></li>
</ul>
<h5><b>Solution</b></h5>
<p>This vulnerability was fixed starting in the following build:</p>
<ul>
 <li><a href="https://www.veeam.com/kb4949" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Veeam Management Pack <i>for Microsoft System Center</i> 13.1 (build 13.1.0.334)</a></li>
</ul>
    </div>
    </div>
</div>
<div class="veeam-text text aem-GridColumn aem-GridColumn--default--12">
    <div class=" veeam-component__component-spacing-below--lg">
    <div class="veeam-text  veeam-text--adaptive-mode" data-component="VeeamTextComponent">
        <h4><b>CVE-2026-107238</b></h4>
<p>A vulnerability allowing an authenticated domain user to perform remote code execution (RCE) as the LocalSystem account on servers running the Veeam Management Pack <i>for Microsoft System Center</i> Collector service.</p>
<p><b>Severity:</b> High<br><b>CVSS v4.0 Score:</b> <span class="veeam-tooltip">8.7<span class="veeam-tooltip-text">CVSS: AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N</span></span><br><b>Source:</b> Discovered during internal testing.</p>
<h5><b>Affected Product</b></h5>
<ul>
 <li>Veeam Management Pack <i>for Microsoft System Center</i> 9.1 and all earlier version 9 builds, including the <a href="https://www.veeam.com/kb4876" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Veeam Backup & Replication 13 compatibility patch</a>.<br><sub><b>Note:</b> A fix will not be provided for version 9.x. Customers running version 9.x should upgrade to 13.1.0.334.</sub><br><sub><b>Note:</b> <a href="https://www.veeam.com/product-lifecycle.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Unsupported product versions</a> were not tested, but are likely affected and should be considered vulnerable.</sub></li>
</ul>
<h5><b>Solution</b></h5>
<p>This vulnerability was fixed starting in the following build:</p>
<ul>
 <li><a href="https://www.veeam.com/kb4949" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Veeam Management Pack <i>for Microsoft System Center</i> 13.1 (build 13.1.0.334)</a></li>
</ul>
    </div>
    </div>
</div>
<div class="veeam-text text aem-GridColumn aem-GridColumn--default--12">
    <div class=" veeam-component__component-spacing-below--lg">
    <div class="veeam-text  veeam-text--adaptive-mode" data-component="VeeamTextComponent">
        <h4><b>CVE-2023-22793</b></h4>
<p>A vulnerability allowing an unauthenticated attacker to perform remote code execution (RCE) on servers running the Veeam Virtualization Extensions service of Veeam Management Pack <i>for Microsoft System Center</i>.</p>
<p><b>Severity:</b> Critical<br><b>CVSS v4.0 Score:</b> <span class="veeam-tooltip">9.3<span class="veeam-tooltip-text">CVSS: AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N</span></span><br><b>Source:</b> Discovered during internal testing.</p>
<h5><b>Affected Product</b></h5>
<ul>
 <li>Veeam Management Pack <i>for Microsoft System Center</i> 9.1 and all earlier version 9 builds, including the <a href="https://www.veeam.com/kb4876" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Veeam Backup & Replication 13 compatibility patch</a>.<br><sub><b>Note:</b> A fix will not be provided for version 9.x. Customers running version 9.x should upgrade to 13.1.0.334.</sub><br><sub><b>Note:</b> <a href="https://www.veeam.com/product-lifecycle.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Unsupported product versions</a> were not tested, but are likely affected and should be considered vulnerable.</sub></li>
</ul>
<h5><b>Solution</b></h5>
<p>This vulnerability was fixed starting in the following build:</p>
<ul>
 <li><a href="https://www.veeam.com/kb4949" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Veeam Management Pack <i>for Microsoft System Center</i> 13.1 (build 13.1.0.334)</a></li>
</ul>
    </div>
    </div>
</div>
</div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
